decimalDigits purpose "The exact decimal digits of (high * 2^64 + low) * 2^exponent, as ASCII without leading zeros (`0` for 0) in a new heap block, with the count and how many of them follow the decimal point stored at an address: 0 the block, 8 the count, 16 the digits after the point"
decimalDigits invariant exactDigits "\"The digits are exactly those of the value, 0.1 being 55 digits all after the point\""
